1) Node** table means “pointer to an array of Node*”
this->table = new Node*[this->capacity];
Breakdown:
Node* = pointer to one linked-list node
Node*[capacity] = array of node pointers
new = allocate memory dynamically
this->table = stores the array address
Why Node*?
Each hash-table slot stores the head pointer of a linked list (separate chaining).
Why Node**?
Because the whole table is an array of Node* pointers.